Protocol Name	P-GSE75189-4	P-GSE75189-1	P-GSE75189-3	P-GSE75189-2															
Protocol Description	TopHat v2.0.13 command line: tophat --transcriptome-index gencode.v19.annotation -T hg19 [fastq file] Cufflinks v2.0.2 command ine: cufflinks -G gencode.v19.annotation.gtf accepted_hits.bam Genome_build: hg19 Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Excel spreadsheet of log2(fpkm+0.01) for protein coding genes	HCT116, HeLa, DLD1, hTERT RPE1 and GBM514 cells were infected with virus carrying the Cas9-2A-Blasticidin expressing cassette and infected cells were selected with blasticidin (5 ug/ml). After 10 days of selection, single cells were sorted onto 96-well plates with a BD FACS Aria IIu cell sorter at low pressure (20 PSI) using a 100 micron nozzle or by manual seeding of a single cell suspension at 0.6 cells/96 well plates. Independent clones were isolated and FLAG-Cas9 expression was determined using Western blot analysis.	RNA was extracted from Cas9-expressing cell lines using TriReagent (Sigma) according to manufacturer's instructions RNA sequencing libraries were prepared with Illumina TruSeq V2 RNA library preparation kit according to manufacturer's directions. Multiplexed libraries (HCT116 only) were sequenced on a single read High Output Illumina NextSeq500 flow cell (version 1 chemistry) with a read length of 61bp.	HCT116 cells were maintained in McCoyâs 5A medium with L-glutamine (Life Technologies) supplemented with 10% FBS (Life Technologies) and 1% Penicillin/Streptomycin (Life Technologies). HeLa, DLD1, and hTERT RPE1 cells were maintained in DMEM with high glucose and pyruvate (Life Technologies) supplemented with 10% FBS (Life Technologies) and 1% Penicillin/Streptomycin (Life Technologies). The patient-derived GBM514 glioblastoma cell line was kindly provided by Peter Dirksâ laboratory at SickKids, Toronto. GBM cells were cultured as described in Pollard et al. 2009.															
